        "original_id": "1f8a7142-af14-58bb-8ca0-db000545360f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: The Periodic Table of Videos, Hello Internet\n- People: Brady Haran, Martyn Poliakoff, Peter Licence, Stephen Liddle, Debbie Kays, Neil Barnes, Sam Tang, CGP Grey\n- Organizations: BBC News, University of Nottingham, YouTube\n- Topics: chemical elements, the periodic table, educational videos, documentary films, podcasts\n\nFacts:\n- Brady Haran was born on 18 June 1976.\n- Brady Haran is an Australian-born British independent filmmaker and video journalist.\n- Brady Haran is known for educational videos and documentary films produced for BBC News.\n- Brady Haran’s notable YouTube channels include Periodic Videos and Numberphile.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is a series of videos about chemical elements and the periodic table.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is published on YouTube.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is produced by Brady Haran, a former BBC video journalist.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos features Martyn Poliakoff, Peter Licence, Stephen Liddle, Debbie Kays, Neil Barnes, Sam Tang, and others at the University of Nottingham.\n- Martyn Poliakoff is identified in The Periodic Table of Videos as “The Professor.”\n- Hello Internet is an audio podcast hosted by CGP Grey and Brady Haran.",
